language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Decide how many templates to print, which design variations each template carries, and how many sheets to print from each template, so that every variation is printed at least its demanded number of copies, minimising the total number of printed sheets.
given n_slots : int(1..)
given n_templates : int(1..)
given n_var : int(1..)
given demand : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_var)] of int(0..)
find layout : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_templates), int(1..n_var)] of int(0..n_slots)
find production : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_templates)] of int(0..max(demand))

branching on [production, layout]

minimising sum(production)

such that
$ each template has at most n_slots design positions, so the copies of all variations on it fit within n_slots
forAll t : int(1..n_templates) . (sum v : int(1..n_var) . layout[t,v]) <= n_slots,
$ each variation must be printed at least as many copies as its order demands, summed over all sheets printed from all templates
forAll v : int(1..n_var) . (sum t : int(1..n_templates) . production[t] * layout[t,v]) >= demand[v],
$ templates are interchangeable, so they are listed in non-increasing order of printed sheets
forAll t : int(1..n_templates-1) . production[t] >= production[t+1],
$ every sheet carries at most n_slots copies, so the total number of copies printed covers the total demand
n_slots * (sum t : int(1..n_templates) . production[t]) >= sum(demand)
